title: Genesis 22 – God Will Provide Himself a Lamb
description: A verse-by-verse study of Genesis 22: Abraham offers Isaac on mount Moriah, a picture of Christ in every detail, here I am and here am I, God will provide himself a lamb, the ram in the thicket, Jehovahjireh, and the faith of Hebrews 11.
output: lessons/genesis/genesis-22-god-will-provide-himself-a-lamb.html
context: Genesis 22

# Genesis series pattern (Genesis 1-5). Slide text is the author's own words from the Genesis 22 study (posts 7116,
# 7117, 7118, 7119, 13 December 2022), set in chapter order. Post 7116 walks the chapter in its own paraphrase with
# the author's notes in brackets; the slides show the KJV verses and keep his bracketed notes, as he wrote them, as
# the commentary on each. 2 Chronicles 3:1, Leviticus 14 and Hebrews 11, which the study names, are shown as cross
# references.
# Fixed: "Issac who carried the wood" -> "Isaac", "God tell Moses 8n Leviticus" -> "in Leviticus" (7117). Nothing else.

=== Introduction
--- Genesis Chapter 22 [title]
overline: Young Adult Sunday School • Genesis Series
heading: Genesis 22: God Will Provide Himself a Lamb
sub: Abraham and Isaac • Mount Moriah • The Ram in the Thicket • Jehovahjireh
refs: Genesis 22:1-24
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse.

=== Mount Moriah
--- Behold, Here I Am
kicker: v. 1
sub: God Did Tempt Abraham
big: Genesis 22:1 | mark: Behold, here I am
p: *Here I am.* (Remember this for later)

--- Thine Only Son Isaac
kicker: v. 2
sub: Get Thee into the Land of Moriah
big: Genesis 22:2 | mark: thine only son Isaac, whom thou lovest; the land of Moriah
p: (2 Chronicles 3:1 tells us that Moriah is where Jerusalem is). *And offer him there for a burnt offering* (Jesus three days and nights in Hell) *upon one of the mountains which I will tell thee of* (Golgotha?)

--- Mount Moriah
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 22:2
fig: 2 Chronicles 3:1 | 2 Chronicles 3:1
callout: Of course the sacrifice of Christ Jesus recalls **Genesis 22**, Abraham and Isaac; the purification sacrifice laid out in Leviticus 14, the mount in Jerusalem being where Abraham brought his son.

--- On the Third Day
kicker: vv. 3–4
sub: He Saw the Place Afar Off
scripture: Genesis 22:3-4 | mark: on the third day Abraham lifted up his eyes
p: *On the third day*, (obvious). (Jesus lifting up his eyes rising up from hell)

--- And Come Again to You
kicker: v. 5
sub: I and the Lad Will Go Yonder and Worship
big: Genesis 22:5 | mark: and come again to you
p: (Abraham had no doubt that even if he slay his son that God would resurrect him).

--- Laid It upon Isaac His Son
kicker: v. 6
sub: They Went Both of Them Together
big: Genesis 22:6 | mark: laid it upon Isaac his son
p: (Isaac the sacrifice carrying wood up the hill of Golgotha in Jerusalem)

--- God Will Provide Himself a Lamb
kicker: vv. 7–8
sub: Where Is the Lamb?
scripture: Genesis 22:7-8 | mark: but where is the lamb for a burnt offering?; God will provide himself a lamb
p: (God literally is providing himself as the lamb for the burnt offering. That's carefully phrased, don't miss it!)

=== The ram in the thicket
--- Abraham Stretched Forth His Hand
kicker: vv. 9–10
sub: Bound Isaac His Son
scripture: Genesis 22:9-10 | mark: bound Isaac his son

--- Here Am I
kicker: v. 11
sub: Abraham, Abraham
big: Genesis 22:11 | mark: Here am I
p: (*Here I am* is where you brought yourself. *Here am I* is a place where you've been brought)

--- Thine Only Son
kicker: v. 12
sub: Now I Know That Thou Fearest God
big: Genesis 22:12 | mark: thine only son
p: (Again. Note Isaac isn't Abraham's only son, he has an older son Ishmael, God is being precise for a reason, this is a picture of Jesus)

--- A Ram Caught in a Thicket
kicker: v. 13
sub: In the Stead of His Son
big: Genesis 22:13 | mark: a ram caught in a thicket by his horns; in the stead of his son
p: (From the crown of thorns to being the burnt offering in place of Abraham's son, God placed his only begotten son)

--- Two Birds Alive and Clean
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 22:13
fig: Leviticus 14:4 | Leviticus 14:4
fig: Leviticus 14:5-6 | Leviticus 14:5-6
callout: Isaac who carried the wood up the hill, to be the burnt offering. God providing the ram, caught by the head in a thicket of thorns. We see God tell Moses in Leviticus that the sacrifice for him that is to be cleansed *two birds alive and clean, and cedar wood, and scarlet, and hyssop.*

--- Everything Points to Jesus
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 22:13, continued
sub: So That the Jews Would Have No Excuse
p: We see the wood of the cross, the scarlet of the blood, and the hyssop, the same used by the Roman guard to give Jesus the vinegar to drink.
p: We see one bird placed in an earthen vessel, as Jesus was placed in flesh. We see it sacrificed and burned, its blood put on the living bird, which is then set free.
p: Everything points to Jesus and everything in the law was a picture of Him to come, so that the Jews would have no excuse. [[Leviticus 14:4-7|Read Leviticus 14:4–7]]

--- Jehovahjireh
kicker: v. 14
sub: In the Mount of the LORD It Shall Be Seen
big: Genesis 22:14 | mark: In the mount of the LORD it shall be seen
p: Amen!

=== In thy seed
--- By Myself Have I Sworn
kicker: vv. 15–18
sub: In Thy Seed Shall All the Nations of the Earth Be Blessed
scripture: Genesis 22:15-18 | mark: And in thy seed shall all the nations of the earth be blessed

--- He That Had Received the Promises
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 22:18
fig: Hebrews 11:17-18 | Hebrews 11:17-18
fig: Hebrews 11:19 | Hebrews 11:19
callout: Much of this study is reposted from one done during the Gospels, around Easter where I covered **Genesis 22**, and other chapters where this sacrifice is a picture of Christ's. It is amazing when you see the OT is just prelude to Jesus and the better treatment He provides. [[Hebrews 11:8-19|Read Hebrews 11:8–19]]

--- Abraham Dwelt at Beersheba
kicker: v. 19
sub: They Went Together
big: Genesis 22:19

--- Bethuel Begat Rebekah
kicker: vv. 20–24
sub: The Children of Nahor
scripture: Genesis 22:20-24 | mark: And Bethuel begat Rebekah

--- Heirs according to the Promise
center: We only need faith to be heirs according to the promise of God.
read: genesis-21-the-bondwoman-and-the-freewoman | Genesis 21
read: genesis-23-the-death-of-sarah | Genesis 23
read: psalms-6-8 | Psalms 6–8 (Psalm 8, the land of Moriah)
